{"pages": [{"id": 13824, "key": "House_of_Habsburg", "title": "House of Habsburg", "excerpt": "The House of <span class=\"searchmatch\">Habsburg</span> (/ˈhæpsbɜːrɡ/; German: Haus <span class=\"searchmatch\">Habsburg</span>, lit. &#039;House of the Hawk&#039;s Fortress&#039; [haʊs ˈhaːbsbʊrɡ] ), also known as the House of Austria", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "European dynastic family", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/svg+xml", "width": 60, "height": 70, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Arms_of_Counts_of_Habsbourg.svg/60px-Arms_of_Counts_of_Habsbourg.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 3543048, "key": "Habsburg_family_tree", "title": "Habsburg family tree", "excerpt": "This is a <span class=\"searchmatch\">family</span> tree of the <span class=\"searchmatch\">Habsburg</span> <span class=\"searchmatch\">family</span>. This <span class=\"searchmatch\">family</span> tree only includes male scions of the House of <span class=\"searchmatch\">Habsburg</span> from 1096 to 1564. Otto II was the first", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "Family tree of the Habsburg family", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 82, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Habsburgenses.JPG/60px-Habsburgenses.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 148301, "key": "Otto_von_Habsburg", "title": "Otto von Habsburg", "excerpt": "Otto von <span class=\"searchmatch\">Habsburg</span> (20 November 1912 – 4 July 2011) was the last crown prince of Austria-Hungary from 1916 until its dissolution in November 1918. In 1922", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "Heir to the Austrian throne (1912–2011)", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 90, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Otto_von_Habsburg%2C_MEP_%281912%E2%80%932011%29.jpg/60px-Otto_von_Habsburg%2C_MEP_%281912%E2%80%932011%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 655756, "key": "House_of_Lorraine", "title": "House of Lorraine", "excerpt": "Lorraine was joined to the House of <span class=\"searchmatch\">Habsburg</span> and became known as the House of <span class=\"searchmatch\">Habsburg</span>-Lorraine (German: Haus <span class=\"searchmatch\">Habsburg</span>-Lothringen). Francis, his sons Joseph", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "Royal house of Europe", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/svg+xml", "width": 60, "height": 73, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Achievement_%28coat_of_arms%29_of_the_House_of_Lorraine.svg/60px-Achievement_%28coat_of_arms%29_of_the_House_of_Lorraine.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 14258412, "key": "Habsburg_Law", "title": "Habsburg Law", "excerpt": "exiled them and confiscated their property. The <span class=\"searchmatch\">Habsburg</span> Law was repealed in 1935 and the <span class=\"searchmatch\">Habsburg</span> <span class=\"searchmatch\">family</span> was given back its property. However, in 1938", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "Law of German Austria in 1919", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 99, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Habsburgergesetz_1919.jpg/60px-Habsburgergesetz_1919.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 2046523, "key": "Karl_von_Habsburg", "title": "Karl von Habsburg", "excerpt": "von <span class=\"searchmatch\">Habsburg</span> (born Karl Thomas Robert Maria Franziskus Georg Bahnam; 11 January 1961) is an Austrian politician and the head of the House of <span class=\"searchmatch\">Habsburg</span>-Lorraine", "matched_title": null, "anchor